{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/916005-endowment-expanded-yellow-dysphoria","id":916005,"title":"[Endowment Expanded] Yellow Dysphoria","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-16T20:40:34-07:00","id":916005,"title":"[Endowment Expanded] Yellow Dysphoria","content":"(This is for Revlid's <i>fantastic</i> Hotel Mascarone.)<br /> <br /> YELLOW DYSPHORIA<br /> This new Figment is widely held to be an offshoot of White Dementia - it, too, changes the relationship between the hunter and their guest, but in a much less healthy way. Success rate is maybe half that of White Dementia, since you have to prevent inductees from clawing out their own eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Jaundiced Eye Flicker (Yellow Dysphoria \u2022)</b><br /> Under the tender ministrations of a cocktail of sleep aids and caffeine, the hunter learns to check out when their guest checks in. In other words, they tend to sleepwalk more than a bit. They treat rolls due to Fatigue as if they were Resolve + Composure rolls to avoid giving in to a derangement, and can spend one Willpower when waking up to immediately check in. Strangely enough, their body treats being checked in as restful, if dreamless, sleep.<br /> <br /> <b>Fulvid Skin Lesions (Yellow Dysphoria \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> By this points, inductees tend to find that their skin itches and feels loose and &quot;crawly&quot; - some of them report that the guest is more comfortable in their skin than they are. While checked in, you lose your Vice and Virtue - instead, pick one derangement to serve as your Virtue, and another to serve as your Vice. If you checked in due to failing a roll to resist a derangement, you immediately fulfil it if you select it as your replacement Vice.<br /> <br /> <b>Aureate Cyranoid Lessons (Yellow Dysphoria \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> A long round of painful shock therapy lets the inductee know that the most unfortunate part of lying is getting caught. Fortunately, their guest is pretty convincing - and who can blame it? While checked in, the hunter is a completely convincing liar - anything (supernatural or mundane) that would detect the truthfulness of their statements always indicates that they sincerely believe everything they say.<br /> <br /> <b>Citrine Double Mind (Yellow Dysphoria \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Few of the hunters that master this level of the Yellow Dysphoria remember the long syringes filled with sickly yellow fluids, or the weeks of schizophrenic ravings that followed the first injections. This level of mental disconnect is only stable if the inductee has the mental split created through Blue Delusion; as such, they need to have the first dot of Blue Delusion to develop Yellow Dysphoria to this level. The results, however, are worth it. Firstly, the guest gains a second Willpower track, with a number of dots equal to the hunter's dots in Yellow Dysphoria; while checked in, the hunter may spend from either pool interchangeably, and may choose which pool gains any Willpower they regain. Secondly, the guest and hunter can spend Willpower separately - they may spend one Willpower from each pool each turn.<br /> <br /> HOW DOES THIS FIT?<br /> You can treat Yellow Dysphoria as White Dementia for the purposes of taking the 4th dots of various Figments - this modifies Red Delirium, removing the memory erasure tied to Willpower unless you <i>also</i> have the first dot of White Dementia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user